msgid "Coding Standards"
msgstr "Coding Standards"

msgid "Nexus follows strict coding standards for quality and safety."
msgstr "Nexus follows strict coding standards for quality and safety."

msgid "C Standard"
msgstr "C Standard"

msgid "C11 for source code"
msgstr "C11 for source code"

msgid "C11 for production code and maintained C contract fixtures"
msgstr "C11 for production code and maintained C contract fixtures"

msgid ""
"C++17 for host GoogleTest/GoogleMock and external ABI consumer checks; "
"neither the test framework nor its C++ runtime enters firmware"
msgstr ""
"C++17 for host GoogleTest/GoogleMock and external ABI consumer checks; "
"neither the test framework nor its C++ runtime enters firmware"

msgid "Code Formatting"
msgstr "Code Formatting"

msgid ""
"The project uses clang-format for automatic code formatting. Run ``clang-"
"format`` before committing code."
msgstr ""
"The project uses clang-format for automatic code formatting. Run ``clang-"
"format`` before committing code."

msgid ""
"See also: ``.kiro/steering/comment-standards.md`` for detailed comment "
"guidelines."
msgstr ""
"See also: ``.kiro/steering/comment-standards.md`` for detailed comment "
"guidelines."

msgid "Indentation"
msgstr "Indentation"

msgid "Use 4 spaces for indentation (no tabs)"
msgstr "Use 4 spaces for indentation (no tabs)"

msgid "Indent case labels inside switch statements"
msgstr "Indent case labels inside switch statements"

msgid "Do not indent preprocessor directives"
msgstr "Do not indent preprocessor directives"

msgid "Line Length"
msgstr "Line Length"

msgid "Maximum line length: 80 characters"
msgstr "Maximum line length: 80 characters"

msgid "Break long lines at appropriate points"
msgstr "Break long lines at appropriate points"

msgid "Braces"
msgstr "Braces"

msgid "Use attached braces (K&R style)::"
msgstr "Use attached braces (K&R style)::"

msgid "Spaces"
msgstr "Spaces"

msgid "Space after control keywords: ``if (``, ``for (``, ``while (``"
msgstr "Space after control keywords: ``if (``, ``for (``, ``while (``"

msgid "No space after function names: ``func()``"
msgstr "No space after function names: ``func()``"

msgid "No space after casts: ``(int)value``"
msgstr "No space after casts: ``(int)value``"

msgid "Two spaces before trailing comments"
msgstr "Two spaces before trailing comments"

msgid "Space around binary operators: ``a + b``, ``x = y``"
msgstr "Space around binary operators: ``a + b``, ``x = y``"

msgid "Pointer Alignment"
msgstr "Pointer Alignment"

msgid "Pointers align to the left (with the type)::"
msgstr "Pointers align to the left (with the type)::"

msgid "Empty Lines"
msgstr "Empty Lines"

msgid "Maximum one consecutive empty line"
msgstr "Maximum one consecutive empty line"

msgid "Use empty lines to separate logical sections"
msgstr "Use empty lines to separate logical sections"

msgid "Naming Conventions"
msgstr "Naming Conventions"

msgid "Functions: ``module_action_object()`` (e.g., ``nx_gpio_port_write()``)"
msgstr ""
"Functions: ``module_action_object()`` (e.g., ``nx_gpio_port_write()``)"

msgid "Types: ``module_type_t`` (e.g., ``nx_result_t``)"
msgstr "Types: ``module_type_t`` (e.g., ``nx_result_t``)"

msgid "Macros: ``MODULE_MACRO_NAME`` (e.g., ``NX_SUCCESS``)"
msgstr "Macros: ``MODULE_MACRO_NAME`` (e.g., ``NX_SUCCESS``)"

msgid "Constants: ``MODULE_CONSTANT`` (e.g., ``NEXUS_UART0_SELECTED``)"
msgstr "Constants: ``MODULE_CONSTANT`` (e.g., ``NEXUS_UART0_SELECTED``)"

msgid "Static variables: ``s_variable_name`` prefix"
msgstr "Static variables: ``s_variable_name`` prefix"

msgid "Global variables: ``g_variable_name`` prefix (avoid when possible)"
msgstr "Global variables: ``g_variable_name`` prefix (avoid when possible)"

msgid "Documentation"
msgstr "Documentation"

msgid ""
"All public APIs must have Doxygen comments. This project uses ``\\\\`` style"
" Doxygen tags (not ``@`` style)."
msgstr ""
"All public APIs must have Doxygen comments. This project uses ``\\\\`` style"
" Doxygen tags (not ``@`` style)."

msgid "Tag Alignment"
msgstr "Tag Alignment"

msgid ""
"Align the description after each Doxygen tag as shown below. Excluding any "
"surrounding code indentation, the description starts at column 21: the tag "
"and its padding occupy 17 characters after the opening comment star::"
msgstr ""
"Align the description after each Doxygen tag as shown below. Excluding any "
"surrounding code indentation, the description starts at column 21: the tag "
"and its padding occupy 17 characters after the opening comment star::"

msgid "File Header Format"
msgstr "File Header Format"

msgid "Every source file must have a file header comment."
msgstr "Every source file must have a file header comment."

msgid "**Header files (.h)** - Minimal format::"
msgstr "**Header files (.h)** - Minimal format::"

msgid "**Source files (.c)** - Full format with version and copyright::"
msgstr "**Source files (.c)** - Full format with version and copyright::"

msgid "Header Files (.h)"
msgstr "Header Files (.h)"

msgid ""
"Header files contain full API documentation including parameters and return "
"values::"
msgstr ""
"Header files contain full API documentation including parameters and return "
"values::"

msgid "Source Files (.c)"
msgstr "Source Files (.c)"

msgid ""
"Source definitions explain hardware ordering and invariants without "
"duplicating ``\\param`` or ``\\return`` from the header. Use ``\\brief``, "
"``\\details`` and ``\\note`` as needed::"
msgstr ""
"Source definitions explain hardware ordering and invariants without "
"duplicating ``\\param`` or ``\\return`` from the header. Use ``\\brief``, "
"``\\details`` and ``\\note`` as needed::"

msgid "Section Comments"
msgstr "Section Comments"

msgid ""
"Use section comments to organize code into logical blocks. The separator "
"line must be exactly 79 characters (``/*`` + 75 characters + ``*/``), "
"preserving the existing template::"
msgstr ""
"Use section comments to organize code into logical blocks. The separator "
"line must be exactly 79 characters (``/*`` + 75 characters + ``*/``), "
"preserving the existing template::"

msgid ""
"**Important**: Do NOT use ``/*===...===*/`` style separators. Always use "
"``/*---...---*/`` for consistency."
msgstr ""
"**Important**: Do NOT use ``/*===...===*/`` style separators. Always use "
"``/*---...---*/`` for consistency."

msgid "Inline Comments"
msgstr "Inline Comments"

msgid "Use ``/* comment */`` style for inline comments, not ``//``::"
msgstr "Use ``/* comment */`` style for inline comments, not ``//``::"

msgid "Macro Comments"
msgstr "Macro Comments"

msgid "Use Doxygen block comments or inline comments for macros::"
msgstr "Use Doxygen block comments or inline comments for macros::"

msgid "Static Functions"
msgstr "Static Functions"

msgid "Static functions use simplified comments with only ``\\brief``::"
msgstr "Static functions use simplified comments with only ``\\brief``::"

msgid "Prohibited Practices"
msgstr "Prohibited Practices"

msgid "The following practices are NOT allowed:"
msgstr "The following practices are NOT allowed:"

msgid "Using ``@`` style Doxygen tags (use ``\\\\`` instead)"
msgstr "Using ``@`` style Doxygen tags (use ``\\\\`` instead)"

msgid "Using ``//`` single-line comments (use ``/* */`` instead)"
msgstr "Using ``//`` single-line comments (use ``/* */`` instead)"

msgid ""
"Using ``/*===...===*/`` section separators (use ``/*---...---*/`` instead)"
msgstr ""
"Using ``/*===...===*/`` section separators (use ``/*---...---*/`` instead)"

msgid "Duplicating ``\\param`` and ``\\return`` in source files (only in headers)"
msgstr ""
"Duplicating ``\\param`` and ``\\return`` in source files (only in headers)"

msgid "Ownership and evidence"
msgstr "Ownership and evidence"

msgid ""
"Public declarations specify context, deadlines, retained storage and failure"
" state. Describe why a volatile read, ordering barrier or drain is "
"necessary. ``SETTLED`` is the provider's final request access. Cancellation "
"never permits reclaiming a borrowed buffer before settlement or proved "
"controlled recovery."
msgstr ""
"Public declarations specify context, deadlines, retained storage and failure"
" state. Describe why a volatile read, ordering barrier or drain is "
"necessary. ``SETTLED`` is the provider's final request access. Cancellation "
"never permits reclaiming a borrowed buffer before settlement or proved "
"controlled recovery."

msgid ""
"Changed files pass whole-file formatting and mechanical comment checks. "
"Install local Git hooks with ``python scripts/setup/install_dev_tools.py``. "
"The commit and CI gates share ``scripts/ci/style_gate.py``; no hook bypass "
"is a validation result. Actual warning/analyzer and behavioral evidence is "
"separate from style."
msgstr ""
"Changed files pass whole-file formatting and mechanical comment checks. "
"Install local Git hooks with ``python scripts/setup/install_dev_tools.py``. "
"The commit and CI gates share ``scripts/ci/style_gate.py``; no hook bypass "
"is a validation result. Actual warning/analyzer and behavioral evidence is "
"separate from style."

msgid ""
"Selected analyzer checks do not establish MISRA certification or industrial "
"functional-safety qualification."
msgstr ""
"Selected analyzer checks do not establish MISRA certification or industrial "
"functional-safety qualification."
